// dyn(0x8000000000000000) <s const 0x9000000000000000 -> 1. Both values are
// non-negative signed-256 (only limb0 set, bit255 clear), so the helper does
// an UNSIGNED limb0 compare: 0x8000... < 0x9000... = 1. Hard gate: an
// erroneous SIGNED i64 limb0 compare would read limb0 as negative.
PUSH8 0x9000000000000000
PUSH32 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000008000000000000000
PUSH1 0x00
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x00
MLOAD
SLT
PUSH1 0x00
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x20
PUSH1 0x00
RETURN
